Dispersion measures how spread out data values are around a centre.
Three measures with formulae:
range $=$ largest value minus smallest value;
variance $\sigma^{2}=\frac{\sum f(x-\bar{x})^{2}}{\sum f}$;
standard deviation $\sigma=\sqrt{\sigma^{2}}$.
